To change user password right click on user a clik reset password then reset password
If account gets locked out you can unlock the account on the same reset password page

If you double click on a specific group you can add people in the members tab (can also remove people too)

Instead of manually adding a new user and doing stuff you can just right click on a user and click on copy
This will add a person to the same group as them 

In the account tab of a user you can unlock account from there, check to see if account is disabled

You can change what OU a user is in by simply clicking and dragging them to the place where they need to be

You can add descriptions to users in the general tab
can also add phone number, email, office, initials, and web page if web page i guess

In the organization tab you can add his title, department, company, and manager name

Telephone tab may contain home number, pager, mobile number, fax, and ip number

Profile tab contains profile path if user has their own directories, can also add logon script 

Attribute editor tab
Best practice is to filter it to have attributes that actually have values, can edit everything from this tab
Another thing if you simply type a letter it'll bring you to where the letter first appears when first

Distribution Group is used for emailing everyone in a certain group

easy way to find something is go to find users, contacts, and groups tab where the arrows are and then change In: users to In: Entire Directory
